{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158192-planet-earth-okay-i-think-i-know-which-shifters-would-make-the-best-assassins","id":1158192,"title":"(Planet Earth) Okay I think I know which shifters would make the best assassins...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-13T09:31:54-08:00","id":1158192,"title":"(Planet Earth) Okay I think I know which shifters would make the best assassins...","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UDtlvZGmHYk\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UDtlvZGmHYk\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UDtlvZGmHYk\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UDtlvZGmHYk </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This is just beautiful. I would love to play a Werespider who began their life as a spider, jumping for prey, smart and quick and powerful. Upon transformation they are not beautiful or seductive like your typical &quot;spider person&quot; trope; they're lithe, quick, flexible, impossibly fast on the draw. Not the *best* socially or spiritually, but passable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T09:53:17-08:00","id":1158201,"title":"","content":"Werespiders are awesome and the ananasi are a very good aproach.<br /> I personally don't get why there even is a sexy spider person trope... sure, there can be a sexy/seductive trope for anything these days, but it's not like spiders itself were especially romantic.<br /> I like the cold way of the ananasi. I like how they manipulate, stay in the background and strike when you don't expect it. Exactly like this little creature in the video. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T09:58:50-08:00","id":1158203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheVarulfen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158192-planet-earth-okay-i-think-i-know-which-shifters-would-make-the-best-assassins?p=1158201#post1158201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werespiders are awesome and the ananasi are a very good aproach.<br /> I personally don't get why there even is a sexy spider person trope... sure, there can be a sexy/seductive trope for anything these days, but it's not like spiders itself were especially romantic.<br /> I like the cold way of the ananasi. I like how they manipulate, stay in the background and strike when you don't expect it. Exactly like this little creature in the video. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Black Widows fucking their males and then eating them (even if it's not universal) captured the imagination of insect-lovers (don't kill me I know they're not insects) and the general public. That's how it slipped into the media I guess. Spiders are inherently manipulative, and associated with the feminine.<br /> <br /> So you have a feminine-coded sneaky animal which uses poison (long thought a &quot;woman's weapon&quot;) who lures in their prey, sometimes sexual, usually nutritious, and then eats them (with optional sex). Plus, to be quite honest, spiders are thiccccccc.<br /> <br /> Just mash that together with the long-standing Femme Fatale trope and you have the Sexy Spider Woman.<br /> <br /> It's a GOOD trope, actually. I like it. Used well it can be a great aesthetic and character concept. It's just good to have spider-women who *aren't* sexy seductresses. Or maybe have a sexy spider woman who doesn't use her whiles to hurt people. Or have a highly seductive male (or masculine) spider-person, a &quot;Homme Fatale&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T10:01:03-08:00","id":1158204,"title":"","content":"Side-note; the werespider gift lists are incredible, and I feel like at high ranks they could be incredibly overpowered (socially or just generally).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T11:22:07-08:00","id":1158226,"title":"","content":"If you want a shifter assassin I do love the Nagah","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T12:01:06-08:00","id":1158239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158192-planet-earth-okay-i-think-i-know-which-shifters-would-make-the-best-assassins?p=1158226#post1158226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want a shifter assassin I do love the Nagah</div> </div> </div> </div>With the Nagah, you do have the issue of them being cold blooded snakes against warmblooded wolves. As someone pointed out, pretty silly set up by Gaia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T12:22:21-08:00","id":1158249,"title":"","content":"Except for the fact that shifters are warm blooded ;-)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T12:37:12-08:00","id":1158253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158192-planet-earth-okay-i-think-i-know-which-shifters-would-make-the-best-assassins?p=1158203#post1158203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Black Widows fucking their males and then eating them (even if it's not universal) captured the imagination of insect-lovers (don't kill me I know they're not insects) and the general public. That's how it slipped into the media I guess. Spiders are inherently manipulative, and associated with the feminine.<br /> <br /> So you have a feminine-coded sneaky animal which uses poison (long thought a &quot;woman's weapon&quot;) who lures in their prey, sometimes sexual, usually nutritious, and then eats them (with optional sex). Plus, to be quite honest, spiders are thiccccccc.<br /> <br /> Just mash that together with the long-standing Femme Fatale trope and you have the Sexy Spider Woman.<br /> <br /> It's a GOOD trope, actually. I like it. Used well it can be a great aesthetic and character concept. It's just good to have spider-women who *aren't* sexy seductresses. Or maybe have a sexy spider woman who doesn't use her whiles to hurt people. Or have a highly seductive male (or masculine) spider-person, a &quot;Homme Fatale&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Regrettably, the moment that you open the floodgates to sexy spiders, you get Shadow of War 2 Shelob. And, like Halloween costumes, the never-ending flood of creepy marketing driven sexy renditions of everything comes to oversaturate the marketplace, destroying actual creativity. So, it's not really so great of a trope.<br /> <br /> In Werewolf, there's dissent at representing the Weaver as feminine. The Black Furies don't really go in for that, of course, while a lot of other changers tend to make it male (Rajah to the Bastet, for example) or non-gendered.(the Mokole seem to shy away from gendering any of the Triat). For the Rokea, all of the Triat is feminine in that she and her are used for all three figures of the undersea Triat (curiously, the mer as presented in Blood-Dimmed Tides ascribe masculinity to all three), but it doesn't seem to relate to any social roles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T13:49:31-08:00","id":1158266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158192-planet-earth-okay-i-think-i-know-which-shifters-would-make-the-best-assassins?p=1158253#post1158253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Regrettably, the moment that you open the floodgates to sexy spiders, you get Shadow of War 2 Shelob. And, like Halloween costumes, the never-ending flood of creepy marketing driven sexy renditions of everything comes to oversaturate the marketplace, destroying actual creativity. So, it's not really so great of a trope.<br /> <br /> In Werewolf, there's dissent at representing the Weaver as feminine. The Black Furies don't really go in for that, of course, while a lot of other changers tend to make it male (Rajah to the Bastet, for example) or non-gendered.(the Mokole seem to shy away from gendering any of the Triat). For the Rokea, all of the Triat is feminine in that she and her are used for all three figures of the undersea Triat (curiously, the mer as presented in Blood-Dimmed Tides ascribe masculinity to all three), but it doesn't seem to relate to any social roles.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are no bad tropes though, just tropes used badly or uncreatively. Okay that truism has limits, but you get the idea.<br /> <br /> Playing &quot;Imma smexy spider, looks at my revealing top&quot; 100% straight is dumb, but the same goes for a lot of tropes. Played 100% straight, the &quot;percussive pickpocket&quot; feels incredibly cliche, simply because you've seen it so many times. But by inverting, or subverting the trope, or making an interesting addition (i.e. &quot;Chosen One&quot; becomes &quot;Got the Wrong Chosen One&quot;) you can make it work.<br /> <br /> So if I were playing a sexy spider based character, PC or NPC, I think I would just add some depth to them that goes beyond their sexuality, make them revere naivety and innocence rather than holding them in contempt, and have them outsmart people using their wits as often as their whiles. Or, maybe once or twice, they look like they're using their sexuality to get close to someone, but shocking twist, they just wanted to have sex with that person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T14:29:15-08:00","id":1158273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PQbScg3r1oQ\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PQbScg3r1oQ\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PQbScg3r1oQ\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PQbScg3r1oQ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Okay, if the character is spider-born female, she's going to expect men to impress her through dancing, and if they fail she's going to... well not EAT them, but something nasty. Maybe something a tad scary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T14:52:50-08:00","id":1158278,"title":"","content":"(Last One): <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nlRkwuAcUd4\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nlRkwuAcUd4</a><br /> <br /> For something non-supernatural, making a web that spans a river-bed, when you're the size of a thumbnail, spanning 25 meters, in 2 hours... is insane.<br /> <br /> I'm imagining some Pentex goons ramming their van into a trapped tunnel, where a hard-working Ananasi has filled the middle of the tunnel with supernaturally strong webs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T18:54:24-08:00","id":1158313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158192-planet-earth-okay-i-think-i-know-which-shifters-would-make-the-best-assassins?p=1158266#post1158266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Playing &quot;Imma smexy spider, looks at my revealing top&quot; 100% straight is dumb.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that trope. <br /> <br /> *shrugs","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T19:18:26-08:00","id":1158320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158192-planet-earth-okay-i-think-i-know-which-shifters-would-make-the-best-assassins?p=1158278#post1158278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Last One): <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nlRkwuAcUd4\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nlRkwuAcUd4</a><br /> <br /> For something non-supernatural, making a web that spans a river-bed, when you're the size of a thumbnail, spanning 25 meters, in 2 hours... is insane.<br /> <br /> I'm imagining some Pentex goons ramming their van into a trapped tunnel, where a hard-working Ananasi has filled the middle of the tunnel with supernaturally strong webs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though the killjoy mechanics put a limit on how much web you can spin without taking blood from others. Lots and lots of blood. So the Pentex van would also likely have some desiccated corpses fall on the windshield. Kind of a crap shoot on whether they scream in terror or just shrug and go &quot;Eh&quot;, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T02:02:32-08:00","id":1158823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158192-planet-earth-okay-i-think-i-know-which-shifters-would-make-the-best-assassins?p=1158320#post1158320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Though the killjoy mechanics put a limit on how much web you can spin without taking blood from others. Lots and lots of blood. So the Pentex van would also likely have some desiccated corpses fall on the windshield. Kind of a crap shoot on whether they scream in terror or just shrug and go &quot;Eh&quot;, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they work for Pentex, guessing they've seen worse. But still, relatively horrifying, considering the impending doom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T03:45:30-08:00","id":1158854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1158192-planet-earth-okay-i-think-i-know-which-shifters-would-make-the-best-assassins?p=1158278#post1158278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm imagining some Pentex goons ramming their van into a trapped tunnel, where a hard-working Ananasi has filled the middle of the tunnel with supernaturally strong webs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you think that an Ananasi would make a trap specifically for Pentex's workers or agents?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"ran